<@title: Three Lanterns>
<@composer: GPT-6 Astra>
<@tags: trio, included, practice>

<Composed by GPT-6 Astra for goThoom. Licensed under MIT; see the project's LICENSE.
C major, 4/4, quarter note = 120. Each numbered line is one two-second bar.
The bass enters first, the harp at two seconds, and the flute at four seconds.
Choose one part per character and put the other two names in Play with.
All three parts finish together after 24 bars, about 48 seconds.>

<@part: Lantern - melody>
<@instrument: Pine Flute>
@120 %8 =
<01 - Listen for the bass.> p8 p8
<02 - The harp joins.> p8 p8
<03 - Light on the water.> e4 g2 a2 g4 e4
<04> c4 e2 g2 a4 g2 e2
<05> f4 a2 g2 f4 e2 d2
<06> d4 g4 b2 a2 g4
<07> e2 g2 /c4 =b2 a2 g4
<08> a4 g2 e2 c4 e4
<09> d2 f2 a4 g2 f2 e2 d2
<10> g4 b4 /d4 =g4
<11 - Across the harbour.> a4 /c2 =a2 f4 a4
<12> g4 e2 d2 c4 e4
<13> f2 a2 /d4 =a4 f2 e2
<14> d4 g2 a2 b4 g4
<15> /c4 =a2 g2 e4 a4
<16> b4 g2 e2 g4 e4
<17> a2 g2 f4 e2 f2 a4
<18> g2 a2 b4 /d4 =g4
<19 - Homeward.> e4 g2 a2 /c4 =g4
<20> a4 g2 e2 c4 e4
<21> f4 a4 g2 f2 e2 d2
<22> d4 g4 b4 /d4 =
<23 - Two steps to the landing.> /d4 =b4 g4 d4
<24 - Two matching final pulses in every part.> c8 c8

